{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2510 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "2e1482fdd106a2d03f1b01e4ae4ac32fc91ac5c7642739742aa3c588f4f2a7b0" :edb/db-before-t 2509 :edb/db-after-t 2510 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535822 50 #inst "2026-10-09T08:08:52.390Z" 13194139535822 true] [17592186198305 1020 #edb/ref 17592186368346 13194139535822 true] [17592186198305 1020 #edb/ref 17592186368353 13194139535822 true] [17592186198307 1020 #edb/ref 17592186368325 13194139535822 true] [17592186198307 1020 #edb/ref 17592186368332 13194139535822 true] [17592186198307 1020 #edb/ref 17592186368339 13194139535822 true] [17592186368325 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368326 13194139535822 true] [17592186368325 1089 "q-161260" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368325 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535822 true] [17592186368325 1100 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u-v,\\,2,\\,{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩.$*" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368325 1113 #uuid "cbf9769b-e719-507c-b9ae-aedbdeda8205" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368325 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩|}_{x=u-v\\,y=2\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2+{v}^{2},\\,u-v+{v}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2+{v}^{2},\\,u-v+{v}^{2},\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =(2+{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+(u-v+{v}^{2})\\cdot (-2v)+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨y+z,\\,x+z,\\,1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2uv+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[-{u}^{2}v+2u{v}^{2}-2u{v}^{3}]_{u=0}^{u=1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-v+2{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3})\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368327 13194139535822 true] [17592186368326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368328 13194139535822 true] [17592186368326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368329 13194139535822 true] [17592186368326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368330 13194139535822 true] [17592186368326 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368331 13194139535822 true] [17592186368326 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535822 true] [17592186368326 1041 "selection" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368326 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368328 13194139535822 true] [17592186368326 1110 #uuid "20917b75-fe62-52ee-a01b-7330211086e4" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368327 1034 "-\\frac{5}{6}" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368327 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535822 true] [17592186368327 1111 #uuid "bc85c7ec-e94f-5cc6-a0a9-71946bc91fac" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368328 1034 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368328 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535822 true] [17592186368328 1111 #uuid "b6265d35-2477-5dff-9a25-0f6b76984398" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368329 1034 "2" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368329 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535822 true] [17592186368329 1111 #uuid "a0c23154-9064-52cf-9d7e-58bc4e9b6e46" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368330 1034 "4" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368330 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535822 true] [17592186368330 1111 #uuid "74a203ec-054c-5784-9824-8a9ab34bfea2" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368331 1034 "-1" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368331 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535822 true] [17592186368331 1111 #uuid "0e12f856-7e17-572a-b616-439001e001e8" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368332 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368333 13194139535822 true] [17592186368332 1089 "q-161278" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368332 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535822 true] [17592186368332 1100 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,-v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $-1\\le u\\le 0$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368332 1113 #uuid "d17f424f-954b-5ecb-a437-f702f864c48b" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368332 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩|}_{x=u+v\\,y=v-u\\,z=-v} \\\\  & =⟨-(u+v)-(-v),\\,u+v-(v-u),\\,-(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-u,\\,2u,\\,v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-u,\\,2u,\\,v⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(-u)\\cdot 1+2u\\cdot 1+v\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-u+2u+2v \\\\  & =u+2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨-x-z,\\,x-y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(u+2v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(u+2v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[uv+{v}^{2}]_{v=0}^{v=1}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(u+1)\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}+u]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368334 13194139535822 true] [17592186368333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368335 13194139535822 true] [17592186368333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368336 13194139535822 true] [17592186368333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368337 13194139535822 true] [17592186368333 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368338 13194139535822 true] [17592186368333 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535822 true] [17592186368333 1041 "selection" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368333 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368335 13194139535822 true] [17592186368333 1110 #uuid "a674a4f2-cd96-5068-b65f-cac49a2431f7" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368334 1034 "3" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368334 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535822 true] [17592186368334 1111 #uuid "ce19b1bd-324d-57c7-be76-e8fe8afe9acf" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368335 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368335 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535822 true] [17592186368335 1111 #uuid "24deb3bc-e5ee-5102-ab5e-233560eedbab" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368336 1034 "-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368336 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535822 true] [17592186368336 1111 #uuid "961ba168-d91b-5bb5-9344-02e1b34f322d" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368337 1034 "-4" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368337 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535822 true] [17592186368337 1111 #uuid "aa962c07-7205-5309-8156-c3c9859c459f" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368338 1034 "\\frac{5}{4}" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368338 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535822 true] [17592186368338 1111 #uuid "e6e3fd14-00cb-5b37-b59b-0c283fe3c88c" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368339 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368340 13194139535822 true] [17592186368339 1089 "q-161283" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368339 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535822 true] [17592186368339 1100 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,2,\\,-3xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by the equations\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u{v}^{2},\\,-1,\\,1-2u⟩\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368339 1113 #uuid "defa14c1-7205-58bc-bb12-6ea263aa0092" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368339 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1-2u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{v}^{2},\\,0,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1-2u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2uv,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {v}^{2} & 0 & -2 \\\\ 2uv & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,-|\\begin{aligned}{v}^{2} & -2 \\\\ 2uv & 0\\end{aligned}|,|\\begin{aligned}{v}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 2uv & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-4uv,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨z,\\,2,\\,-3xy⟩|}_{x=u{v}^{2}\\,y=-1\\,z=1-2u} \\\\  & =⟨1-2u,\\,2,\\,-3(u{v}^{2})(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-2u,\\,2,\\,3u{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨1-2u,\\,2,\\,3u{v}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-4uv,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =(1-2u)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot (-4uv)+3u{v}^{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-8uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,2,\\,-3xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-8uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-8{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}uv\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-8{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{0}^{1}v\\,\\text{d}v\\, \\\\  & =-8\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-8(\\frac{1}{2})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535822 true] [17592186368340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368341 13194139535822 true] [17592186368340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368342 13194139535822 true] [17592186368340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368343 13194139535822 true] [17592186368340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368344 13194139535822 true] [17592186368340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368345 13194139535822 true] [17592186368340 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 131